Parts adapted from Trellis
--------------------------

The one-criterion-per-reviewer design, and the wording of the substantiveness, correspondence and
paper-faithfulness rubrics, are adapted from Wes Pegden's Trellis
(https://github.com/wpegden/trellis; arXiv:2606.09674). The following parts are licensed under the
PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
(https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0), not under Apache-2.0:

  - audits/AUDIT_PROTOCOL.md, the sections "Lane A — Substantiveness", "Lane B — Correspondence"
    and "Lane C — Paper-faithfulness" (the project root's AUDIT_PROTOCOL.md that install.sh
    creates is a link to this file);
  - the reviewer prompts cut from those sections: the substantiveness, correspondence and
    paper-faithfulness lane prompts that audits/prompt.py extracts from them and writes into a
    run's audit record (<round>/prompts/).

